codex
The Jira evidence describes a deterministic persistence/restart boundary bug in affected ZooKeeper 3.3.4: a maximum-size client payload is accepted, but its serialized transaction is seven bytes larger (`1,048,583`) and then rejected during database reload. I’m specifying a single-node restart test and the ordinary three attempts; no race/flakiness evidence supports increasing the count.
